      "attack_scenario": "During market volatility where a collateral's SPOT price drops 30-50% below its EMA (no circuit breaker prevents this during liquidation), an authorized liquidator calls `liquidate_as_coin` on a just-underwater obligation; the SPOT-price-based seizure formula over-seizes collateral relative to the debt reduction in EMA terms, leaving the obligation at a worse risk ratio than before and enabling repeated liquidations that drain the borrower's collateral beyond what is economically justified.",
      "checklist_id": "PROP-01b-partial1-post-003"
    },
    "text": "After liquidation, risk_level must improve (decrease) toward or below 100%.",
    "assertion": "forall liquidate(oblig): post(risk_level(oblig)) < pre(risk_level(oblig))",
